specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:130:Any other field is ignored, and the validator forwards only the fields the frame defines. In particular the server does not read a `chatId` from this message: the connection already determines the session ([validated by: drops any field the frame does not define, rather than forwarding it](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L18)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:132:An empty, blank, or over-length `user_message` is answered with `INVALID_MESSAGE` and `stream_end` ([validated by: answers an empty user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L473), [validated by: answers a blank user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L477), [validated by: answers an over-length user_message with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L481)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:142:- A session processes one `user_message` at a time, in the order the frames arrived: a frame arriving while an earlier one is still running waits, and its answer starts only after the earlier run's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a second user_message only after the first has sent its stream_end, in the order they arrived](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L755)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:143:- The waiting message's model request therefore holds the earlier answer finished, never one still streaming ([validated by: hands the second run a history whose first answer is finished, never one still streaming](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L786)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:144:- A `ping` is answered at once, even while a run is pending ([validated by: answers a ping at once while a run is pending](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L804)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:145:- A frame that fails validation and is not a `user_message`, such as a malformed `ping`, gets its `INVALID_MESSAGE` at once, even while a run is pending, but a `user_message` that fails validation is answered in turn, its `INVALID_MESSAGE` and `stream_end` after the run in progress, since an `error` frame names no message and would otherwise read as the running answer's ([validated by: answers an invalid ping at once but an invalid user_message in turn, after the run in progress](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L817)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:146:- The reconnect flush (§ 11.3), which sends queued messages in one burst, is therefore safe: they are answered one after another, in the order the user typed them ([validated by: queues three messages sent in one tick before the handler returns, and answers them in that order](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L833)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:147:- A queued message whose socket has closed by the time its turn comes is dropped, neither recorded nor answered, since nobody is left to read the answer and a session whose last socket closed has no credentials left ([validated by: drops a queued message whose socket closed before its turn, without asking the model or recording it](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L850)).
